; `->` in the tape layout, for a rule that is a node of the tape with children of its own (it holds a number, so
; the layout opens it and does not make it one text entry): the rewrite rolls the tape back to the opener and the read of
; the template writes the node again, closer and all.
prefix none
whitespace none

cond = name as A " > " num as B " AND " num as C         -> A " > " B " AND " A " > " C
     | rel " AND " rel
     | rel
rel  = name " > " num
name = 1*0x61..0x7a
num  = int
